[Music]  last summer I was visiting family in  Singapore when I got a text message we  respond to Miami love yesterday thanks  not knowing the number I respond with  the usual sorry who is this  Adam s comes response thanks for not  realizing thanks for not realizing  that's obnoxious but whatever I'm gonna  be polite here so I respond with sorry  what's your full name I don't see any  emails from you to which he responds  Adam losing patience Solar Adam losing  patience Solar are you serious like who  are you I'm being patient with you your  first strike was thanks for not  realizing but this one's really pushing  it where are your manners so I pulled my  phone I frustrated and be like let me  teach you how to spell losing cuz you  clearly didn't go to primary school  instead I paused and I showed the text  message to my younger brother who read  it and said wait a minute  I think dad works for an atom solar and  then it dawned on me I was boring my dad  SIM card in Singapore so I must have  been texting his coworkers so I run to  dad is from the phone be like dad I  think I'm talking to your to your  friends there and he reads the  conversation looks up and says poke it  I'm glad you're not the angry puppy that  used to be otherwise today I'd be  looking for a new job this experience  first introduced me to the notion that  emotional intelligence is extremely  important in the business workplace  it can literally save your job and turns  out there's a lot of data to support  this Daniel Goleman who writes about  this in the Harvard Business Review  arrives at this conclusion  he says emotional intelligence matters  more and more to higher up you get in a  company in fact the difference between a  star performer and an average performer  is 90% attributable to emotional  intelligence consider the following two  examples where a lack of emotional  intelligence was quite harmful uber CEO  Travis kalanick  got in a fight with an uber driver on  video the uber driver is seen telling  cowl neck that he lost ninety seven  thousand dollars and went bankrupt  because rubra changed his policies and  reduced fares cowl-neck then yells back  saying some people don't like to take  responsibility for their own [ __ ] they  blame everything on somebody else this  outburst cost kalmyk personally two  hundred thousand dollars and eventually  contributed to him losing his job or  consider Elon Musk  when British diver Vernon Unsworth  publicly criticized Elon Musk's ideas on  Twitter musk lashed back calling him a  pedophile and a child rapist this led to  a prolonged media crisis and a lawsuit  my point is that I should be the CEO of  Tesla and uber  but in all seriousness as we progress in  our careers we'll be faced by situations  and people that test our patience more  and more frequently and in those  situations the cost of not handling that  with poise will also increase so it's of  paramount importance that we work on our  emotional intelligence before we go out  and change the world so you're probably  wondering now how do I do this well  there's two important parts of the brain  that need to be trained sequentially the  first is the neocortex the neocortex  handles logic so if you want to learn  Excel you read a book and now you know  how to use Excel it learns quickly the  limbic system handles emotions this  one's a little slower to teach something  to the limbic system we need consistency  or practice over a long time so how  about we take the first step together  let's train our neocortex and let's take  the example of anger so first our aim  here is to convince the neocortex that  in some situations anger is  counterproductive so in the case of the  text messages when I get angry  I'm excreting chemicals in my body that  are literally poisoning my system in  other words I'm drinking the poison and  I'm hoping that the guy on the other  side of the text message gets hurt so  what does the neocortex say to this  illogical in the case of Travis kalanick  we need to understand that anger is not  helping him drive towards objective if  anything is pushing him further away not  only did he fail to convince the uber  driver of his side of the argument he  also lost a lot of money and eventually  his job so what is the neocortex side of  this again illogical and in the case of  Elon Musk we need to understand that if  he lets every hater online get him  bothered then boy is he gonna live a  terrible life in this case he may not  have lost his job but he will definitely  lose his peace of mind every time a  bully picks up a phone and fires off a  tweet so hopefully by now your neocortex  is convinced that  some situations anger is  counterproductive now comes the hard  part the limbic system because you can  convince your neocortex or something but  your limbic system will say I'm still  angry  I still have anger now I've been working  on this for a while like you remember my  dad said as an angry child and I found  the pro methodology to work really well  for me the peon Pro stands for pause  pausing in a difficult situation gives  you time to act instead of reacting so  when I go to text message I was able to  pause and gather more information and  then act as opposed to reacting with an  equally sassing message the RN Pro  stands for a reframe when uber CEO  Travis kalanick heard those words he  took that as a personal affront to him  instead he could have reframed those  words as product feedback coming from a  very important company constituents the  drivers had he done that he could have  probably avoided the 2019 uber strike  that happened right before the IPO and  the OM Pro stands for own own your  emotions and in my opinion the most  important one currently we blame the  external circumstances for internal  emotions so we're constantly trying to  fix the external world to fix our  internal world but the reality is that  our influence on the external world is  heavily limited so Owen means to go from  an external locus of control for  emotions to an internal locus of control  for emotions so Elon Musk did not get  angry because somewhere some person  hated on him on Twitter he got angry  because internally he was attached to  the idea that no one should criticize  him publicly and by changing that  expectation he can change his emotional  state  so how about we handle this situation  like a pro  and pause reframe maybe a spilling juice  oliver myself makes this more  entertaining for you and there'll be  more views and own  I'm not feeling what I'm feeling right  now because that's flow juice over  myself it's because I had an expectation  internally that this talk go flawlessly  so my point is that when in these  situations anger is not the only thing  that can be worked on with Pro you can  also do this with disappointment with  hatred with sadness any other emotion so  I hope that you walk out of this room  and next time you're faced with a  challenging situation you evaluate the  merit of the emotional reaction and then  you pause you reframe and you own thank  you  [Applause]  [Music]

